BigBlueButton published its three bbb-web advisories on 2026-05-13, and BSI's advisory followed on 2026-05-18; no source names DFN, SWITCH, GÉANT, Swiss cantonal schools or German education ministries as BigBlueButton operators. The checksum bypass lets any user send valid requests to some endpoints without a checksum, and the SSRF, which needs a high-privilege user, exposes private-address assets only if the attacker has gained additional access.
